<Item XName="READ_ME" UserName="READ_ME" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;P style=&quot;BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in; BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-TOP: 0in&quot; class=MsoTitle align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-SIZE: 18pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;VTB_64QAM&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoBodyText align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = o /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-pagination: widow-orphan lines-together&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;This workspace is similar to the &lt;STRONG&gt;VTB_Example&lt;/STRONG&gt; tutorial workspace elsewhere in SystemVue, except that this also includes two additional RF PAs to measure locally before exporting to ADS as a Verification Test Bench.&amp;nbsp; It can be used to see the flow back &amp;amp; forth between SystemVue and ADS.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-pagination: widow-orphan lines-together&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;One of the PA models is an X-parameter device, exported from a 850MHz celluar amplifier example often used in ADS as for demonstrations.&amp;nbsp; The other is its behavioral equivalent, a compressing dataflow amplifier with a nominal gain of 12.95dB and a input 1dB compression power of about +16dBm (ie - P1DB=28dBm).&amp;nbsp; In addition, this workspace can be used as a VTB in ADS to test the original transistor-level amplifier using Circuit Envelope, and compare the results.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-pagination: widow-orphan lines-together&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The 3 simulation results should be fairly comparable, as long as you match the &lt;STRONG&gt;power levels &lt;/STRONG&gt;and &lt;STRONG&gt;impedance loading&lt;/STRONG&gt; conditions here.&amp;nbsp; Based on load-pull simulations, the X-parameter device was loaded here in the Spectrasys subcircuit with ZL=32ohms to give optimal PowerOut; the dataflow simulation really doesn&apos;t know about voltages and currents and just assumes ZL=50ohms.&amp;nbsp; In ADS, you will want to play with both&amp;nbsp;input power and load impedance to see their effects.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-pagination: widow-orphan lines-together&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;THINGS TO TRY HERE&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-pagination: widow-orphan lines-together&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;1. 3 parameters have been marked for mousewheel up/down &quot;tuning&quot;:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-pagination: widow-orphan lines-together&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Modulation Type &lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;(4=16QAM, 6=64QAM, 8=256QAM)&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-pagination: widow-orphan lines-together&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;RF input power level &lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;(Pin=16dBm --&amp;gt; P1DB point)&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-pagination: widow-orphan lines-together&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;X-parameter load impedance &lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;(32=best Pout, 50=0.5dB lower)&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-pagination: widow-orphan lines-together&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;2. If you want to use this as a VTB, deactivate the RFLINK and AMPLIFIER device models in this workspace, and then activate the SVE_LINK model that&apos;s in the middle.&amp;nbsp; Then save the workspace your local working directory.&amp;nbsp; Close SystemVue, run ADS,&amp;nbsp;and import the .WSV file into ADS using the instructions for &quot;Custom VTB&quot;s in that product.&amp;nbsp; It becomes a VTB library that is local within your open ADS workspace.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-pagination: widow-orphan lines-together&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;LICENSES REQUIRED&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-pagination: widow-orphan lines-together&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;In SystemVue, this simulation just uses a basic license.&amp;nbsp; If you simulate the X-parameter device, you will need the W1719 RF Sys license.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-pagination: widow-orphan lines-together&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;In ADS, this VTB just requires either a &quot;VTB Engine&quot; or &quot;Ptolemy&quot; license; along with Harmonic Balance and Circuit Envelope for the circuit co-sim.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-pagination: widow-orphan lines-together&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-pagination: widow-orphan lines-together&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;FURTHER INSTRUCTIONS/TUTORIALS&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-pagination: widow-orphan lines-together&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;For more information on how to create VTB designs please refer to the following sections of the SystemVue documentation:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-pagination: widow-orphan lines-together&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;Simulation &amp;gt; Verification Test Bench (VTB)&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-pagination: widow-orphan lines-together&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;Tutorials &amp;gt; Verification Test Bench Tutorial&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;The VTB designs included in this workspace are:&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;U&gt;EVM_Measurement&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;This VTB design performs an EVM measurement on a modulated signal. The symbol rate of the signal is fixed at 0.2 MHz. Several modulation formats can be selected and modulation impairments can be added to the signal.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;When adding impairments&amp;nbsp;(IQ Offset, Gain and Phase Imbalance) the constellation plot (EVM_Meas_Tx_Constellation) may seem inconsistent with the trajectory one (EVM_Meas_Tx_Trajectory). For example, applying an offset only along the x-axis might show (in the constellation plot) as offset along the other axis, both axes, or the expected axis but in the&amp;nbsp;opposite direction. The reason is that the constellation plot uses data generated by the EVM sink, whereas the trajectory plot uses data created by just filtering the signal with a Root Raised Cosine filter. The EVM sink performs demodulation on the input signal and may arbitrarily rotate it by any angle that is an integer multiple of the angle to which the constellation is phase invariant (rectangular QAM constellations are 90-degree phase invariant and Star-QAM constellations are 45-degree phase invariant).&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;U&gt;ACPR_Measurement&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;This VTB design demonstrates how to post-process simulation data in a VTB design.&amp;nbsp; It measures ACPR for a modulated signal. The symbol rate and the modulation format of the signal can be set using VTB parameters. The modulated signal goes through a non-linear amplifier whose output 1 dB compression point is also controlled by a VTB parameter.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;ACPR is measured by computing the spectrum power in different bands using a custom ACPR function defined inside the SystemVue workspace. &lt;STRONG&gt;This ACPR function is for demonstration purposes only. It does&amp;nbsp;NOT comply with any standard. &lt;/STRONG&gt;Four user defined variables have been created in the dataset (MyACPRMinus1, MyACPRMinus2, MyACPRPlus1, MyACPRPlus2) that are calculated by calling the ACPR function. This function takes as arguments data created by the simulation (S2_Power, and S2_Power_Freq) as well as values computed based on the top level design parameters (FCarrier, SymbolRate). To get these parameters in the dataset you need to check the &lt;EM&gt;Save Design Parameters to Dataset&lt;/EM&gt; check box in the &lt;EM&gt;Options&lt;/EM&gt; tab of the Data Flow analysis.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;</Text>
